Designed with ultra-thin armor plating and an advanced Electronic Camouflage system, "Nightclub" can actively manipulate its surface color and texture to blend directly into dark surroundings. It features a sleek, angular silhouette with minimal exterior protrusions, allowing it to move almost completely silently while baffling active radar and infrared tracking systems.

In Iron Man 3, Tony manually equips "Nightclub" during the climax at the Norco oil rig to fight Aldrich Killian directly. Demonstrating high-speed martial arts combat, Tony uses the suit's speed to deliver several strikes before Killian manages to overpower the armor, driving his superheated hand straight through the chest arc reactor and forcing Tony to eject.
